title: Veeam: Configuration backup
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the configuration backup of a Veeam Backup & Replication
 server, collected via the Veeam special agent. It reports whether
 configuration backup is enabled, the time since the last successful backup,
 the number of restore points kept, whether encryption is enabled, and the
 target repository.

 This check is {WARN} by default if configuration backup is disabled; the
 state is configurable, since deliberately not using configuration backup is
 a valid choice for some customers. It is {CRIT} if configuration backup is
 enabled but no successful backup has ever been recorded.

 {WARN} and {CRIT} levels can be set for the time since the last successful
 backup.

discovery:
 One service is created per host, provided the Veeam special agent was able
 to fetch the configuration backup settings from the API (this endpoint
 requires an Administrator credential until version 13.2).
